{"step_index":4977,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T14:29:53Z","thinking":"PROC-006 shows a net gain of 10 matches compared to PROC-005; however, there were 18 new matches added and 8 removed/moved. Examining the 'Needs Review' metric is crucial for understanding the nature of these changes. I will focus on 'Needs Review' in relation to the overall match increase.\n\n\nAnalyzing the 33 items in \"Needs Review\" to assess the rationale behind their classification. Initial investigation of Item 1 identifies distinct drug names and formulations (Rosecef/Primrose vs. Duricef), validating the review placement due to potential confusion.\n\n\nDeduction: Accurate OCR match identified; drug names, manufacturer, and formulation align perfectly, warranting inclusion.\n\nReasoning: Considering potential syrup substitutions, distinct formulations require pharmacist review to verify the appropriate Bronchophane alternative due to varying ingredients (Guaifenesin vs. Dextromethorphan).\n\nEvaluation: Considering a possible OCR error, the names 'Flub' and 'Flavir' warrant review due to similarity.\n\nDecision: Rejecting the distinct Helicek (Omeprazole) and Helicure (multi-drug kit) match, a pharmacist's input is needed, due to the different trade names.\n\nAssessment: Despite similar function, potential OCR issues with Depovit (Amoun) and Depopen (MUP) justify further review.\n\nConclusion: 'Moist 1' and 'I am' cream should undergo pharmacist review due to potential confusion in product identification.\n\n\nThe \"متاسيل\" entry likely represents an OCR error, misreading \"ستلاسيل.\"  No psychiatric medication \"متاسيل\" exists, reinforcing this hypothesis.\n\n\"يوكيراتو\" and \"يوريكير\" creams are both urea-based; a match is likely but requires further confirmation. The \"سينوبريت\" vs \"سينوريت\" difference is likely OCR-related; the presence of \"ب\" indicates \"Sinupret.\"\n\n\"ريتشي بانثينول\" and \"يوريتشي بانثينول\" represent similar formulations. \"اوبتك سالين\" and \"اوبست\" need confirmation due to potentially different eye drops.\n\n\"فاتروكسيم\" and \"زروكسيمور\" show potential drug name confusion, so the OCR needs further checking. \"ايزيس ينسون\" requires consideration due to the flavored version.\n\n\nVolume discrepancies between \"ماجيك اويل\" (60ml vs. 120ml) necessitate review.  \"هيرو دي3+كي2\" and \"هيدرو في اي دي تري كيه\" drops are a confirmed match. \"بروتولوك\" and \"كونترولوك\" are the same drug (Pantoprazole), different brands; pharmacist review needed.\n\nI suspect OCR issues again, for items like \"فيتا زنك\" and \"فيتا زون,\" \"ليفست\" and \"ليفوستام,\" or \"برونكوفين\" and \"برونكوف.\"  Discrepancy in \"باروفين\" points to a mismatch between Paracetamol + Ibuprofen (Parofen) and a different strength of Parofen.\n\n\nReviewing the \"باروفين\" entry, the system incorrectly flagged it due to a presumed typo, failing to recognize the exact match in both the requested and candidate items; this requires correction.\n\nRecognizing the OCR omission, the 'يوريفين فوار' vs. 'يورين فوار' case constitutes a true OCR catch, requiring immediate action to align this case with a match.\n\nLevanic and Tavanic, both containing Levofloxacin, represent a straightforward match despite differing names, and should be corrected to be matched.\n\nAnalysis of 'ايموكسكلاف' reveals a concentration discrepancy, with OCR likely misreading the strength; further manual review to verify the concentrations should be considered.\n\n\nStrength discrepancies between \"200mg\" and \"400mg\" necessitate a review.\n\nAn OCR error likely caused \"اسبوسيد أطفال\" to be misread as \"استوسيد أطفال\"; a true OCR catch, requiring immediate action to align this case with a match.\n\n\"Starkopina 5mg\" and \"Starcoprex 5mg\" are from the same company and require pharmacist review due to potential confusion in product identification.\n\n\"Zurcal 20mg\" (Pantoprazole) and \"Zoracan\" (Fluconazole) are different drugs, necessitating a pharmacist review.\n\n\"Kerovit\" (multivitamin) and \"Nerovit\" (B-complex) represent different drug types, requiring pharmacist review.\n\nThe system incorrectly matched \"ابيكوتيل\" and \"البوتيل\"، which are different drugs; this must be corrected. \"برونكوفين\" and \"برونفين 400mg\" require evaluation of formulations.\n\n\nExamining the system's incorrect match of \"Epicotil\" and \"Albothyl\"; these represent distinct medications, requiring correction. The inappropriate \"Bronchophane syrup\" and \"Brufen 400mg tablet\" matching necessitates reevaluation due to formulation differences. Further review is necessary for the accurate identification of drug type, form, and concentration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Investigate strange matches in El Makromy","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import openpyxl\n\nwb6 = openpyxl.load_workbook(r'D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\processes\\PROC-006\\results_PROC-006.xlsx', data_only=True)\nws = wb6['المكرومي المنصورة.pdf']\n\nfor row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    if any(k in str(row[0]) for k in ['ابيكوتيل', 'برونكوفين']):\n        print(f\"Shortage: '{row[0]}' | Warehouse: '{row[1]}' | Grade: '{row[2]}'\")\n","Description":"Check El Makromy matches for epicotil and bronchophane","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\check_makromy_odd.py","toolAction":"Writing odd match check script","toolSummary":"Write check_makromy_odd.py"}}]}
